```python
def delete_at_position(head, pos):
    if head is N/A or pos < 1:
        return head
    if pos == 1:
        return head.next  # delete head
    curr = head
    for _ in range(pos - 2):
        if curr is N/A:
            return head  # position exceeds length
        curr = curr.next
    if curr is N/A or curr.next is N/A:
        return head
    curr.next = curr.next.next
    return head
```
A wrong answer that doesn't check `curr.next is N/A` before `curr.next.next` reveals the student ignores the "position exceeds list length" edge case, causing AttributeError.
